            <ArticleTitle>Saphenous vein graft growth 13 years after coronary bypass in a child with Kawasaki disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1127-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presumed limited growth potential of saphenous vein grafts has led many authorities to discourage their use in young children. We documented excellent growth and patency of a saphenous vein graft 13 years after operation in a 7-year-old child with coronary artery obstruction caused by Kawasaki disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
